 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Texture-Based Octree Rendering
-A rendering technique that uses an octree built around bricks of a certain size [S2, unofficial]. Cuts of the octree are reconstructed into textures and sent to the GPU for volume rendering [S2, unofficial]. The octree lookup process was a bottleneck in early implementations, resulting in sub-interactive frame rates for medium-sized (256^3) volumes [S2, unofficial]. This method differs from Texel-per-Node Encoding by focusing on the rendering pipeline's use of brick-based textures rather than the storage format of the octree nodes themselves [S2, unofficial]. It is chosen when out-of-core GPU paging is required, and links to [SVO Node Encoding](2705-svo-node-encoding.md).
